<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.993 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.993 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$3.3 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due June 12 was 2.993 percent, up from 2.943 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.5 billion of 182-day T-bills due September 11, 1997 was 3.285 percent, up from 3.245 percent last week, and on C$1.1 billion of 357-day T-bills due March 5, 1998 was 3.743 percent, up from 3.649 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$525 million three-month, C$125 million six-month and C$100 million one-year bills. It holds C$800 million of C$5.1 billion of bills due March 20. Details follow  </p>
